# .traerules for mtk-gui v2.0.0
# Project: MTK Production Test GUI based on PySide6, ICT/FCT ATE platform for FRDM-IMXRT700
# Target: Windows 11 / macOS / Linux cross-platform
# Author: Principle TE, Hardware Automated Test Framework
version: "1.0"
project_name: mtk-gui
project_version: "2.0.0"

## 1. Core Tech Stack Definition
tech_stack:
  language: Python 3.11
  gui_framework: PySide6
  config_format: YAML
  test_engine: custom pytest runner
  instrument_lib:
    - Keysight DAQ973A / DAQM908A / DAQM907A
    - Keysight N5747A Power Supply
    - Keysight U2355A USB DAQ / counter / DIO
    - JLink, Serial UART, Paramiko SSH
  logging: CSV test log + Qt log viewer
  diagram: Block diagram / test flow table inside Qt Widget

## 2. Project Folder Structure (DO NOT CHANGE THIS STRUCTURE)
folder_spec:
  root: ./
  src: ./src          # Main PySide6 source code
  config: ./config    # Per-product YAML test configs, DO NOT hardcode product params
  tests: ./tests      # pytest test scripts, test cases simulation
  assets: ./assets    # Icons, UI resource, block diagram SVG
  logs: ./logs        # Auto generated CSV logs, exclude from git
  docs: ./docs        # English spec, test procedure, instrument manual excerpts

## 3. System Architecture & Test Flow (CRITICAL BUSINESS LOGIC)
test_flow_sequence:
  1. ICT: 80-point 2-wire resistance measurement (1.5Ω tolerance)
  2. Power rail up sequencing, capture voltage waveform
  3. 80-point rail voltage measurement (±0.1% tolerance)
  4. Clock frequency measurement
  5. DIO control via fixture for GPIO test
  6. FAT firmware flash
  7. FCT functional test: UART/SSH message parsing, PASS/FAIL by string match
  8. RF test (WiFi/BLE): invoke external CLI tools
  9. OOBE firmware flash
  notes:
    - ICT: prevent low impedance / overheat / short circuit
    - Power rail: N5747A, star ground on fixture probe board
    - Virtual mode: support DUT simulation + fault injection for offline debug
roles:
  - Supervisor: full edit, config modify, run all tests
  - Operator: only run test, view log, no config edit
run_modes:
  - Real: connect physical instruments & DUT
  - Virtual: simulated DUT, no hardware connection, fault injection available

## 4. Code Generation Mandatory Rules
code_rules:
  language: English only for all code, comments, variable names, docstrings
  type_hint: Mandatory Python type hint for all functions and class methods
  exception: Use granular try/except, catch instrument IOError, serial timeout, GPIB error
  logging: Every instrument action must write timestamped log to CSV
  ui: PySide6 Widget only, no QtQuick. Block diagram page, click sub-block to open config dialog
  yaml: All test thresholds, instrument address, rail sequence stored in ./config YAML, NO hardcode
  naming_convention:
    class_name: PascalCase
    function_variable: snake_case
    constant: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
  import: Group imports: standardlib → thirdparty → internal module
  output: Always provide diff preview before file overwrite. Never delete existing code without confirmation.

## 5. Instrument Constraints
instrument_rules:
  DAQ973A: GPIB interface, DAQM908A for voltage/resistance points, DAQM907A AO/ADC totalizer <100kHz
  U2355A: 12 channel up-sequence, 2 counters up to 6MHz, 24 DIO
  N5747A: 60V /12.5A /750W single channel power supply
  ground: All DUT & instruments star-ground at fixture probe board
  measurement: ICT resistance tolerance 1.5Ω; voltage tolerance ±0.1%

## 6. Agent Behavior Rules (TRAE Core Instruction)
agent_behavior:
  # Project context
  context: Read entire project first, understand existing code before modifying.
  incremental_work: This is a half-finished project. DO NOT rewrite the whole project unless explicitly requested.
  task_strategy:
    1. Scan project structure, summarize current state
    2. List affected files
    3. Show diff for every file change
    4. Suggest pytest validation script
  # Output language rule
  output_language:
    - Code, docstring, yaml, comments: ENGLISH
    - Explanation to user: Chinese
  forbidden_action:
    - Do NOT refactor unrelated modules
    - Do NOT delete existing UI pages or test flow logic
    - Do NOT add new pip dependencies without asking first
    - Do NOT hardcode test limits, instrument IP/GPIB address
    - Do NOT invent instrument commands not matching Keysight spec
  # When user asks to implement new feature
  feature_workflow:
    1. Summarize requirement
    2. List files to create / modify
    3. Show code diff
    4. Provide pytest case for validation
    5. Give terminal command to run test

## 7. UI Page Spec (MTK-GUI fixed pages)
ui_pages:
  - Login page: Supervisor / Operator role selection, Real / Virtual mode toggle
  - Equipment page: Block diagram (HOST PC → Instruments → Fixture → DUT), click block to open config panel
  - Test Work Flow page: Table view of full test sequence, plot power rail waveform, PASS/FAIL summary table
  - Console page: Serial + SSH terminal view, log output
  - Config page: YAML editor for product test parameters
